    "title": "Children with notes",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM baseline WHERE Notes IS NOT NULL",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Children with notes endline",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM endline WHERE Notes IS NOT NULL",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average height by gender",
    "sql": "SELECT Gender, AVG(\"Height cm\") AS avg_height FROM baseline GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "Gender",
    "y": [
     "avg_height"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average height by location",
    "sql": "SELECT Location, AVG(\"Height cm\") AS avg_height FROM baseline GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "Location",
    "y": [
     "avg_height"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Height trend",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Child ID\", \"Height cm\" FROM baseline ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "\"Child ID\"",
    "y": [
     "\"Height cm\""
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The fitness programme has {{p1}} children participating. Of these, {{p3}} have notes from the baseline survey, and {{p4}} have notes from the endline survey. The average height of children by gender is {{p5.n}} cm for females and {{p5.n+1}} cm for males. The average height of children by location is {{p6.n}} cm in {{p6.x}} and {{p6.n+1}} cm in {{p6.x+1}}. The height of children has increased over time, with an average increase of {{p7.n}} cm from the baseline to the endline survey."
